 "content_notes": "Closed case: Rudolph pleaded guilty in April 2005 and is serving life without parole. The bombings, the park, the victims, injuries and any explosion are never depicted, and no bomb or backpack is drawn; the toll is a typed card in a quiet room. Victims are not named in narration; the memorial is the last spoken line. Rudolph appears only as an anonymous rim-lit silhouette (not a likeness, never his booking photo), never posed heroically, and none of his words or beliefs are quoted. The arresting officer is a generic, unnamed figure (not a likeness). The store, its dumpster, the jail and the mountains are generic drawings with no name, logo or sign; the wanted notice on the jail wall is our own blank design with no seal or face. Every card is our own typed graphic; no real police, court or FBI material is imitated. The security guard who was wrongly suspected in 1996 (and cleared) is left out for pace. No dialogue is invented. Legal status verified 2026-10-12.",
